{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"For a partial-year outage of **n days**, ResStock randomly chooses a start date within the location’s **Building America heating months or cooling months**, as appropriate. It uses **`building_id` as the random seed**, so the selection is reproducible. The outage can extend beyond the season if its duration exceeds the season’s length.\n\nWhere the corresponding Building America months do not exist, ResStock assumes:\n\n- **Heating:** December through February.\n- **Cooling:** June through August.\n\nSource: *ResStock Technical Reference Guide, 2025 Release 1*, §8.4.7, “Unavailable HVAC Periods,” p. 153 ([PDF](https://natlabrockies.github.io/ResStock.github.io/assets/trd/ResStockTechnicalReferenceGuide_2025_1.pdf#page=172))."}}
